// routePermissions is the single table route -> required authorization of the Capsule router (docs/permissions/SPEC.md 9.3 and
// MIGRATION.md 8). It feeds the TokenGate (middleware/tokengate.go) and tests check it against the mounted router,
// routes_authz.golden (the old actions of every route) and the x-permission of docs/permissions/API.openapi.yaml.
//
// Key: "METHOD /full/path" with the chi pattern ("ANY" = every method). Value:
//   - KindPerm: the route needs ALL of Perms (atoms of the catalog). When a route used to check several old actions the handler
//     chooses at run time; the atom listed here is the minimum the route needs and the handler may ask for more (GET .../env asks
//     envvar:reveal with ?reveal, security alerts ask security:triage/admin by severity, promotion approval is decided by the
//     approver list). A scoped token must hold every listed atom.
//   - KindMember: any member of the organization (membership only, as today).
//   - KindSession: any authenticated session; a scoped token never passes.
//   - KindPublic: no user authentication (shared secret and protocol endpoints included).
//
// Planned rows are routes of API.openapi.yaml that P5-P6 will mount (P4 mounted templates, groups, assignments, /me/permissions, simulator and audit); they are here so the table already is the contract.
// Generated from routes_authz.golden by the P3 mapping (docs/permissions/P3-NOTES.md) and maintained by hand afterwards.
